## Contract
Provides basic printf utility functions for integer output, formatting, and array printing.

## Dependencies
none

## Slots
- `print_int(int val)` — prints an integer value
- `print_newline(void)` — prints a newline character
- `print_space(void)` — prints a single space character
- `print_array(int arr[], int n)` — prints an integer array with space-separated values

## Boundaries
- Single-file C implementation
- No dynamic memory allocation
- Array printing assumes valid pointer and count

## Examples
```
print_int(42);        // outputs: 42
print_newline();      // outputs: \n
print_space();        // outputs: (space)
print_array([1,2,3], 3); // outputs: 1 2 3
```

[code]
```c
// Basic printf utilities

void print_int(int val) {
    printf("%d", val);
}

void print_newline(void) {
    printf("\n");
}

void print_space(void) {
    printf(" ");
}

void print_array(int arr[], int n) {
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        printf("%d", arr[i]);
        if (i < n - 1) printf(" ");
    }
}
```
[/code]